WEBVTT

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:29.860
<i>You wanna know something about this bridge?</i>

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:32.060
<i>People call it the “Bridge of Tears.”</i>

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:36.300
<i>The road towards the world of pro boxing will be filled with hard times and suffering.</i>

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:39.580
<i>You might have to shed even more tears than you’ve shed thus far.</i>

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:40.310
<i>But...</i>

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:43.010
<i>they won't be the tears of a loser.</i>

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:46.110
<i>So, Joe, let's grit our teeth together.</i>

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:48.740
<i>And let’s cross this Bridge of Tears in the </i>opposite<i> direction!</i>

00:02:57.970 --> 00:02:59.220
<i>Joe...</i>

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:03.730
<i>People call it the “Bridge of Tears.”</i>

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:05.190
<i>Where people’s dreams are shattered by life.</i>

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:07.100
<i>And when they get exhausted with their lives,</i>

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:09.620
<i>all those sorts of people flow here to Slum Town.</i>

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:12.230
<i>They cross over this sad bridge with tears in their eyes.</i>

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:21.260
The first time I crossed this bridge...

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:24.230
I remember that the wind was pretty strong.

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:28.100
But I never would have thought that I would be living here.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:31.460
I was just looking for a place to eat.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:44.460
After the wind died down and I came to,

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:48.850
I was planning on heading somewhere more decent, wherever my legs took me.

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:55.670
If that hadn't happened...

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:57.910
<i>You bum!</i>

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:01.360
<i>We don't have any free booze to give you!</i>

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:05.450
That was the first time I met old man Danpei.

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:10.200
Back then, the old man was a perfect example of life's gutter-dwellers.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:12.720
I hated his type more than anything.

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:21.700
<i>Hold it right there, kid.</i>

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:23.650
<i>Can you lend me some money?</i>

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:35.290
<i>Don't touch me!</i>

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:38.300
<i>What'd you say!?</i>

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:40.250
<i>You bastard...</i>

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:41.800
<i>Don't mess with me.</i>

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:05.740
<i>Son of a...</i>

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:06.990
<i>Stop right there!</i>

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.000
<i>You've got good form!</i>

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:20.320
Then he held my arms down tightly,

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:22.340
and asked, "You wanna do boxing?"

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:25.760
He said it so clearly, you would hardly think he was the leech of society.

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:29.840
That was my first encounter with the old man,

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:32.510
and my first taste of boxing.

00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:43.030
Cross the Bridge of Tears in the opposite direction?

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:44.830
That does sound nice, old man.

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:04.370
Just the man I was looking for.

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:09.720
I just wanted to see how you were doing after having left the Juvenile prison.

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:13.990
You sure got balls to drop by in the middle of the night.

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:15.770
Eh, Mr. Guerilla?

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:20.570
Come on. I'd take any risk to see how my fellow inmates are doing.

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:22.510
Night or day don't matter.

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:26.170
Especially with you!

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:35.070
Whether it was just courage out of ignorance or a strong nerve...

00:06:35.070 --> 00:06:38.310
You quite honestly impressed us.

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:41.640
<i>S-Senpai... I'll be joining you starting today.</i>

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:43.000
<i>Please forgive us!</i>

00:06:43.570 --> 00:06:45.220
<i>What about you, runt?</i>

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:48.680
<i>Although it is presumptuous for me to name myself, having been asked...</i>

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:50.680
<i>I-Idiot!</i>

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:53.460
<i>I was born not knowing my parents,</i>

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:56.260
<i>and I've lived alone as long as I can remember.</i>

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:58.290
<i>My punch has been strong since I was a child.</i>

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:00.650
<i>No one would dispute that!</i>

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:03.970
<i>On top of all that I was sent to this island.</i>

00:07:03.970 --> 00:07:08.590
<i>I'm the renegade, the lone wolf, Yabuki Joe!</i>

00:07:08.590 --> 00:07:10.660
<i>That's about it. Any questions?</i>

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:15.160
<i>Senpai, please forgive this idiot!</i>

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:23.670
The Juvenile prison was so rough that even Nishi, boss of the holding facility, was afraid.

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:29.090
You were the first and last person to arrive with such indifference.

00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:47.150
You were a fine stray dog.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:58.620
What is it?

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:01.080
Nothing.

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:02.570
What's wrong?

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:08.840
I'm a little disappointed that the same Joe is being kept as a pet here.

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:10.840
A pet!?

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:13.810
Yeah. To think that you would bandage me up.

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:16.850
You're not acting like yourself.

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:21.620
Now that you're given a place to sleep comfortably, you've basically got a leash on you!

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:23.480
Don't you think there's something wrong with that?

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:31.920
Seems like I'm right.

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:33.320
G-Guerilla!

00:08:33.850 --> 00:08:35.400
Don't you get it?

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:38.170
"Go for it, Joe!"

00:08:39.650 --> 00:08:41.290
"Joe, Champion of Tomorrow!"

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:46.940
And all the congratulatory high jinks.

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:50.810
With all this nice treatment, you've become their little pet!

00:08:50.810 --> 00:08:55.010
A stray dog doesn't live in one place and receive compassion.

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:58.110
Eh? Somewhere along the line, you stopped being a stray dog.

00:08:58.110 --> 00:09:02.220
I feel that when you did that, you stopped being yourself.

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:11.900
I really was truly happy last night.

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:15.670
Nishi, Sachi, Tarou, Kinoko, and old man Danpei...

00:09:15.670 --> 00:09:19.980
And everyone in Slum Town gave me such warm looks.

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:23.060
It was the first time it ever happened to me.

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:24.820
And it felt wonderful.

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:28.250
<i>Come on, have a drink!</i>

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:29.750
<i>Oopsie...</i>

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:31.590
<i>Delicious!</i>

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:33.090
<i>Isn't it?</i>

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:06.250
Are you trying to rain on my parade, Guerilla?

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:09.340
Don't threaten me, Joe.

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:11.750
I'm not trying to rain on your parade.

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:17.970
But how long do you think it'll last?

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:21.220
Won't it all just go out like a firework?

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:22.900
That's what I thought, at least.

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:25.310
And that's why I've been travelling around.

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:28.270
As a stray dog, I won't get bummed if it all goes away.

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:31.280
And if I get betrayed, I won't be left heartbroken.

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:32.640
You've been chained down, Joe.

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:36.680
You've been bound hand and foot with these chains.

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:39.360
A stray dog loses its freedom when it's chained.

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:41.240
However...

00:10:41.730 --> 00:10:46.070
When you're like me, wandering around Japan with a guitar in my hand,

00:10:46.070 --> 00:10:49.830
you can really feel the freedom of a stray dog.

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:53.950
Isn't that how men like us are supposed to live?

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:56.120
That's what I think.

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:01.840
You'd better hide.

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:04.690
Use the ladder.

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:05.850
Thanks!

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:09.130
A stray dog, huh?

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:11.860
I'm opening up!

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:15.860
Whoa, that's bright!

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:18.070
Uh, are you alone?

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:19.390
No.

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:21.930
The old man and my friend are sleeping upstairs.

00:11:22.890 --> 00:11:24.120
Upstairs?

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:25.920
What do you want this late?

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:29.580
Oh, we've got reports that a criminal is on the loose in the area.

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:31.050
That must be troublesome, officer.

00:11:31.050 --> 00:11:34.360
You said it. It's not what I want to deal with this late.

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:35.730
Well, be careful.

00:11:41.330 --> 00:11:42.740
Guerilla, you're safe now.

00:11:43.630 --> 00:11:44.390
Thanks.

00:11:44.860 --> 00:11:45.790
So...

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:47.890
Being on the run is how a stray dog lives?

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:49.920
I wouldn't say I'm on the run.

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:53.940
The pigs just decided to chase me around.

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:59.940
Well if you wanna lie low for a few days, there's an abandoned bunkhouse on the sandbank by the river.

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:01.950
A sandbank? That sounds good.

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:05.100
It should be fine if you're suggesting it. I'll go there.

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:05.810
Yeah.

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:07.910
But you know...

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:14.020
I wouldn't say this place is top-class, but it must be easy living here.

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:17.660
Even good old Nishi is fast asleep up there.

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:20.910
Just get going already.

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:23.430
I'll meet you there soon.

00:12:23.870 --> 00:12:28.510
You better bring food with you. I'll expect that much from you.

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:32.480
A stray dog's lifestyle, huh?

00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:42.200
A stray dog's lifestyle, huh?

00:13:02.650 --> 00:13:05.680
Ever since I was little, I've always lived the way I wanted.

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:19.860
<i>Ready!</i>

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:24.110
<i>That idiot!</i>

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:27.240
<i>Where does he think he's going?</i>

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.620
<i>What's going on, Joe?</i>

00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:36.280
<i>Ouch...</i>

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:39.680
After I escaped from the orphanage,

00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:45.350
I started wandering across the nation, from Hokkaido to Kyushu.

00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:47.050
For a small child like me to survive...

00:13:47.050 --> 00:13:49.390
I had to find food without depending on others.

00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:53.550
At the end of that road came the juvenile prison.

00:13:53.550 --> 00:13:56.240
Within those cold, boring cells,

00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:59.360
I received boxing instructions from the old man.

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:00.990
Now that I think back,

00:14:00.990 --> 00:14:04.440
it was a great source of comfort in my loneliness.

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:06.450
<i>Yabuki. Letter for you.</i>

00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:20.390
<i>For the Sake of Tomorrow #1: Left Jab.</i>

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:22.170
<i>What the hell is this!?</i>

00:14:48.010 --> 00:14:51.260
<i>For the Sake of Tomorrow #2: Straight Right.</i>

00:15:06.140 --> 00:15:07.760
It was about that time...

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:09.780
that I met him.

00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:10.800
His name was...

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:12.640
Rikiishi Toru.

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:22.480
<i>The pigs are stampeding!?</i>

00:15:20.690 --> 00:15:22.480
<i>What's going on!?</i>

00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:28.520
<i>Out, out, out, out of my way!</i>

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:34.950
His name was Rikiishi Toru.

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:37.370
He always stood in my way.

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:41.840
<i>Get out of the way!</i>

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:43.050
<i>Move!</i>

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:02.620
Rikiishi...

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:08.880
Most of the people slammed in the juvenile prison are just run-of-the-mill stray dogs...

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:12.070
But he alone was a fine dog who loved boxing.

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:17.120
Compared to him, you're a stray dog through and through.

00:16:20.900 --> 00:16:24.750
And so, the first time you stood in the prison's ring with Rikiishi...

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:27.700
the first time you put on the gloves...

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:31.920
Rikiishi was a fallen boxer who could have been the champ,

00:16:32.660 --> 00:16:35.010
while you were a scarred brawler.

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:38.510
The gap between your skills seemed obvious.

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:54.650
<i>Way to go! Get him!</i>

00:17:13.270 --> 00:17:15.550
<i>He did it! He's down!</i>

00:17:15.550 --> 00:17:16.400
1!

00:17:16.400 --> 00:17:17.360
2!

00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:18.440
3!

00:18:03.760 --> 00:18:04.500
<i>Bring it.</i>

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:58.170
But with strong tenacity...

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:00.040
you managed to pull off a draw.

00:19:00.040 --> 00:19:01.580
The Cross Counter.

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:03.610
That sent a chill down everyone's spines.

00:19:03.610 --> 00:19:05.830
It was such a cool move.

00:19:10.870 --> 00:19:14.340
Compared to that, you're in a real pathetic state.

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:22.960
Oh, these heavy iron chains...

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:24.760
What the hell do you know?

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:28.020
What do you mean by that?

00:19:28.020 --> 00:19:32.020
I'm sure you saw my match with Aoyama.

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:36.980
Back then, I realized...

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:39.010
And you saw...

00:19:39.770 --> 00:19:43.000
When I started defending like some pathetic turtle...

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:44.290
That was...

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:47.300
after I had been beat down again and again by Aoyama.

00:19:47.300 --> 00:19:49.620
It was something I learned naturally.

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:53.920
Boxing defenses, footwork, the clinch, the swayback, ducking.

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:55.210
Boxing defenses, footwork, the clinch, the swayback, ducking.

00:19:55.210 --> 00:19:58.790
Defense makes use of the chance created while attacking.

00:19:58.790 --> 00:20:04.240
I fell in love with the endless depth and breadth of boxing.

00:20:04.240 --> 00:20:05.260
I just couldn't help it.

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:16.900
<i>Joe...</i>

00:20:18.620 --> 00:20:19.750
<i>I'm sorry...</i>

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:27.600
<i>I just wanted to teach you the importance of defense...</i>

00:20:33.850 --> 00:20:35.490
Well, take care.

00:20:35.490 --> 00:20:38.800
I'm gonna settle down here, and start my training tomorrow.

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:41.800
In that run-down shack under the bridge?

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:45.460
As you're chained down and whining like a dog?

00:20:45.460 --> 00:20:47.960
Give it up. That's not you.

00:20:47.960 --> 00:20:50.980
Come on. Join me on my journey.

00:20:50.980 --> 00:20:54.770
Then a life of freedom will be ours.

00:20:55.280 --> 00:20:57.020
How about it, Joe?

00:20:57.700 --> 00:20:59.780
Give it up, Guerilla.

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:03.000
If you know all about that lifestyle, why are you inviting me?

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:06.030
If you're a stray dog, why don't you go running off alone, like a stray dog should?

00:21:09.270 --> 00:21:11.910
You know you can't live up to your smooth talking,

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:14.780
so you've come to find someone who would run away with you.

00:21:14.780 --> 00:21:19.670
Sorry, but there's someone I must beat at all costs.

00:21:31.310 --> 00:21:33.400
Rikiishi Toru.

00:21:33.400 --> 00:21:35.440
Until I defeat him...

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:37.040
I can never be free.

00:22:21.840 --> 00:22:22.850
Well...

00:22:23.370 --> 00:22:25.240
Guess I'd better get going.

00:22:29.140 --> 00:22:30.870
I'm jealous, man.

00:22:32.200 --> 00:22:36.470
You can bare your fangs with all your might.

00:22:36.470 --> 00:22:38.560
You're a true stray dog.

00:22:38.560 --> 00:22:41.210
You bare your fangs and bite down on something.

00:22:41.750 --> 00:22:44.550
That's the sign of a true stray dog.

00:22:51.660 --> 00:22:54.000
I don't know when we'll meet again,

00:22:54.000 --> 00:22:57.730
but I intend to have become a true stray dog by then.

00:22:59.220 --> 00:23:03.370
I don't know where he'll be, but I'm gonna find...

00:23:04.110 --> 00:23:08.090
my own Rikiishi Toru!

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:39.310
"Let's cross the Bridge of Tears in the opposite direction."

00:23:39.310 --> 00:23:41.680
Today, Joe starts afresh.

00:23:41.680 --> 00:23:44.900
Joe has begun training to become a pro.

00:23:44.900 --> 00:23:49.420
But my Tange Boxing Gym doesn't have a professional license.

00:23:49.420 --> 00:23:52.560
Now, for Joe, who is blocked by the greatest wall in his path,

00:23:52.560 --> 00:23:53.790
which way is tomorrow!?
